# A ROAD THROUGH ROCK — plan 20 `A9`, and its acceptance is a PICTURE.
#
# ⚠ THE COUNTS ARE SOMEBODY ELSE'S JOB. `lib/hex_editor/tests/cave.loft` owns the
# rule — thirteen tests over the column's shape, the headroom, the walk, the axis and
# the negative control — and `tools/gates/world/cave.mjs` owns *does the gesture reach
# it*, in `15:` columns and a soffit count. What NEITHER can answer is the only
# question left: **does a person call it a road under an overhang.** That is a cold
# recognition test, and this tree has the scar — `A8.3`'s door passed every count and
# read as a hole for four days, with the verdict delivered twice against the wrong
# object before anyone zoomed in.
#
# So: shoot the shelf ALONE, close, and from the two places an author actually
# stands — beside it looking at the mouth, and on the road looking along it.

echo --- CONTROL: a road on flat ground, which is what an open cut looks like
# ⚠ THIRTY UNITS CLEAR OF WHERE THE MOUNTAIN GOES. A road's slope limit is 1 and the
# raise brush enforces it, so a control road laid where the summit is about to be
# holds the whole mountain down to a ramp — measured through the gate, thirteen
# shelves became one. The control was deciding the subject.
at 0 -30 0
send 10:1
at 4 -30 0
at 8 -30 0
at 12 -30 0
at 16 -30 0
at 20 -30 0
wait rebuilt
send 10:0
step 20
at 10 -22 0
step 30
snap a9-control-open-cut
# nothing here has an underside: an open cut is open
mesh soffit 0 0

echo --- A MOUNTAIN — fourteen strokes, because grass has to stop being grass
# ⚠ `cave_stands` HANGS OFF `tr_face`, so a flank soil can stand on has no rock in it
# to leave overhead. Six strokes is the hill the road gate uses and it is not enough;
# fourteen puts the flank well past 41°.
at 0 0 0
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
key ArrowUp
wait rebuilt
step 20

echo --- AND THE ROAD WALKED ALONG ITS FLANK, not over it
# ⚠ ALONG, AND `probe/house/cave.loft` IS WHY. On a contour the strip is half cut and
# half fill, so the cut has a TRANSVERSE gradient and the uphill cells have rock to
# keep; up the fall line the transverse spread is **1** and there is no cliff side to
# roof at all. ⚠ And z = 7 is swept rather than chosen: 5 gives five shelves, 7 and 9
# give thirteen.
at 0 7 0
send 10:1
at 4 7 0
at 8 7 0
at 12 7 0
at 16 7 0
at 20 7 0
at 24 7 0
at 28 7 0
at 32 7 0
wait rebuilt
send 10:0
step 20
# The rock over the road, DRAWN — its underside is the ceiling `emit_ground_ceiling`
# hangs under the ground, and an open cut has none. This is the count the gate owns;
# it is repeated here only so a picture that looks wrong can be told from a scene that
# was never built.
mesh soffit 100 100000

echo --- THE GALLERY, from the valley — the only angle that can say it
# ⚠ FOUR ANGLES WERE READ BY EYE FIRST AND EVERY ONE WAS AMBIGUOUS, which is why the
# gate carries a number and this file carries a caption. A mountain shot from far
# enough away to see all of it is a silhouette; shot from inside the gallery it is a
# wall of rock either way; and shot from the road at eye level the ceiling is out of
# frame entirely, because a low wide mouth seen from just inside shows nothing but
# daylight. What reads is from OUTSIDE, from the valley, high enough to see the band
# cut into the face and low enough that the rock above it is still overhead.
at 30 9 180
step 10
at 22 12 -110
send 40:1
send 3:0,-600
step 25
snap a9-gallery-from-the-valley

echo --- AND THE EAST END, where the lid stands out over the road
at 26 11 -140
send 40:1
send 3:0,-600
step 25
snap a9-overhang-east

echo --- FROM UNDER IT, looking at the back wall of the cut
# ⚠ APPROACHED ALONG THE ROAD, NOT TELEPORTED IN FROM ABOVE, and the difference is
# the whole picture. `ground_under` asks `world_surface` with the feet it already has,
# so a placement that arrives from over the summit finds the ROCK and stands on the
# roof — measured, twice, and both shots were of a hilltop. Coming along the road
# keeps the reference low and the walker lands on the shelf.
at 20 9 180
step 10
at 18 6 -90
send 40:4
step 25
snap a9-under-the-rock
